{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"cda6fcb7-aa13-46f8-909a-5f9a7e433d6c","title":"Area between two curves"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"cda6fcb7-aa13-46f8-909a-5f9a7e433d6c","step":{"id":"s1","script":"To find the area between two curves, first identify where they cross. Here we compare y equals x with y equals x squared.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Area between two curves"},{"op":"figure","id":"graph","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-0.1,1.15],"y":[-0.1,1.25],"axes":"edge","x_label":"x","y_label":"y"},"marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"line","y":"x","domain":[0,1.1],"label":"y = x"},{"kind":"fn","id":"parabola","y":"x^2","domain":[0,1.1],"label":"y = x²"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"crossings","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"x=x^2\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x=0,\\,1"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"cda6fcb7-aa13-46f8-909a-5f9a7e433d6c","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Between zero and one, the line is above the parabola. Shade only the region trapped between them.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"regionfill","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"shade","between":["line","parabola"],"from":0,"to":1},{"kind":"point","id":"start","at":{"on":"line","x":0},"label":"(0, 0)"},{"kind":"point","id":"finish","at":{"on":"line","x":1},"label":"(1, 1)"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"order","anchor":{"el":"crossings","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"x\\ge x^2\\qquad (0\\le x\\le 1)"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"cda6fcb7-aa13-46f8-909a-5f9a7e433d6c","step":{"id":"s3","script":"A thin vertical strip has height top minus bottom. Adding these strips gives the integral of x minus x squared.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"strip","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"top","at":{"on":"line","x":0.5}},{"kind":"point","id":"bottom","at":{"on":"parabola","x":0.5}},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"bottom"},"to":{"at":"top"},"label":"height"},{"kind":"segment","from":[0.5,0],"to":{"at":"bottom"},"stroke":"dashed"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"integral","anchor":{"el":"order","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"A=\\int_0^1(\\text{top}-\\text{bottom})\\,dx=\\int_0^1(x-x^2)\\,dx"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"Why do we subtract x² from x on this interval?","expected_gist":"The line is above the parabola, so strip heights are x minus x²."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"cda6fcb7-aa13-46f8-909a-5f9a7e433d6c","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Evaluate the antiderivative at the intersection limits. The shaded region has area one sixth of a square unit.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"result","anchor":{"el":"integral","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"A=\\left[\\frac{x^2}{2}-\\frac{x^3}{3}\\right]_0^1=\\frac12-\\frac13=\\boxed{\\frac16}"},{"op":"figure","id":"arearesult","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"text","at":[0.73,0.63],"text":"A = 1/6","size":"small"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
